    "standardized_narrative": "For the 2022 financial year, Syndicate 1856 reported a strengthening of prior year reserves by GBP 5.6 million, representing a 3.37% increase relative to opening gross claims outstanding. This strengthening was primarily due to an additional risk premium applied above the core best estimate reserve to close the 2020 and prior years of account into the 2021 year of account. Additionally, reserves for COVID-19 exposures from the 2019 and 2020 underwriting years, primarily in property reinsurance, saw a GBP 2.5 million strengthening during 2022. The syndicate also incurred significant losses from current year catastrophe events, including Hurricane Ian (GBP 86.8m gross), MidWest Storms (GBP 15.2m gross), and the Russia-Ukraine Conflict (GBP 43.5m gross reserve).",
